tellraw @a {"text": "Technology: The Iron Pillar of Delhi", "color": "gold", "bold": true}
tellraw @a {"text": "The Delhi pillar at 1:1 with a bloomery beside it.", "color": "white"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Gupta India, c. 400 CE", "color": "yellow"}
tellraw @a {"text": "A 7.2-metre, 6-tonne pillar of wrought iron forged from many blooms, standing in the open", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "for 1,600 years with almost no rust.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "The iron is high in phosphorus (about 0.25 percent) and low in sulphur; in Delhi's dry", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "climate a thin, adherent layer of crystalline iron hydrogen phosphate forms and seals the", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "surface. The pillar was built up by hammer-welding hot lumps of bloomery iron, which no", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "European forge could then do at this size.", "color": "gray"}
